<title>UK: Pound surges as budget fuels UK rate-rise hopes.</title>
<headline>Pound surges as budget fuels UK rate-rise hopes.</headline>
<byline>Swaha Pattanaik</byline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sterling surged to its highest levels in five years against the mark, gaining more than three and a half pfennigs as fears that UK Chancellor of the Exchequer Gordon Brown would deliver a draconian budget proved unfounded.</p>
<p>Expectations that interest rates will ratchet higher in the coming months wer kept alive as traders decided Brown had not done enough to curb runaway consumption or to take the wind out of the buoyant housing market's sails.</p>
<p>This will give sterling the fuel it needs to top 2.95 marks, its old European exchange-rate mechanism parity, analysts said.</p>
</text>
